    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "WHAT THIS DOES NOT SAY. It does not claim a FIELD: there is no inverse, no division, no square root, no completeness and no algebraic closure, and none of those is one of the nine. It does not claim an order -- see F:complex-admits-no-compatible-order, which refutes one. It does not retire any Real axiom: the Real package is an ORDERED ring and Complex is not a model of it, only of its equality-only fragment. And Eq Complex is not on offer as equality of complex numbers; Complex.Equiv is.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
      "provenance": {
